            <div xml:id="d754">

                <pb facs="0614" n="498" xml:id="pg498"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/23427.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Mediators.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 8, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    receipt of the note of your excellencies communicating a cablegram which you
                    have received from General Huerta. In reply I beg to say that the troops and
                    munitions mentioned were sent only to Vera Cruz, a place occupied by the United
                    States when your offer of mediation was accepted. I am pleased to inform your
                    excellencies that no aggressive measures of any kind have been taken by this
                    Government since the acceptance of your generous good offices and that nothing
                    has been done in conflict with the understanding with your excellencies as to
                    suspension of hostilities.</p>
                <p>I avail [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
